    "q-73019": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73019",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{8!\\,5!}{3!\\,4!\\,6!}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that $8!=8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6!$ and $5!=5\\cdot 4!$ . Then, we can cancel the $6!$ and $4!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8!\\,5!}{3!\\,4!\\,6!} & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6!\\cdot 5\\cdot 4!}{3!\\cdot 4!\\cdot 6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot \\cancel{6!}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{3!\\cdot \\cancel{4!}\\cdot \\cancel{6!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 5}{3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{140}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
