    "q-19873": {
      "dom_id": "step-q19873",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{89!\\,82!}{90!\\,81!}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that $90!=90\\cdot 89!$ and $82!=82\\cdot 81!\\,.$ Then, we can cancel the $89!$ and $81!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{89!\\,82!}{90!\\,81!} & =\\frac{89!\\,\\cdot 82\\cdot 81!}{90\\cdot 89!\\,\\cdot 81!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{89!\\,}\\cdot 82\\cdot \\cancel{81!}}{90\\cdot \\cancel{89!\\,}\\cdot \\cancel{81!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{82}{90} \\\\  & =\\frac{41}{45}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
